Contract: callers must be able to detect a missing row with `errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound)`. The implementation is:

```go
var ErrNotFound = errors.New("not found")

func LoadRow(id string) error {
    if !exists(id) {
        return fmt.Errorf("load %s: %v", id, ErrNotFound)
    }
    return nil
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
